{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/480378-the-west-other-supernaturals-in-the-wyld-west","id":480378,"title":"The West: Other Supernaturals in the Wyld West","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-14T10:09:25-07:00","id":480378,"title":"The West: Other Supernaturals in the Wyld West","content":"Since today is the 155th Anniversary of the Pony Express. I'm expanding on what the Wyld West books suggested. How do you run the other settings in the Wyld West?<br /> <br /> Here's my thing.<br /> <br /> Vampire: St. Louis is about as far west they want to risk going to. They stay on the eastern side of the country at all times. Those who risk heading west has it coming to them.<br /> Mage: They combat the Storm Umbra in their own ways. The Sons of Ether are on the rise and about to split from the Technocracy.<br /> Wraith: Necropoli spring into existence as fast as the boom towns fall. Fights for resources and to live against the Third Maelstrom rages across the world.<br /> Changeling: European Fae and Nunnehi battle one another for territory. With the rapid expanse from the east, the Nunnehi are on the verge of experience their own version of the Sundering.<br /> Hunter: No Imbued Hunters at the time. Those who find out what goes bump in the night gather posses to hunt down and kill what's out there. Some to protect their families, some for profit.<br /> Kuei-Jin: They start to claim Dragon Nests in California, battling Garou and Magi for their claims. The Kuei-Jin find out quickly how the Sunset people operate.<br /> Mummies: None of have risen. Their loyal cultists seek out new territory and places of power for their respected master (either Egyptian, South American, or Asian).<br /> Demon: Only the Earthbound are available. A couple of reliquaries are discovered in the West, one close to the city of Deadwood, another by a miner party in Colorado where the only survivor is tried and hanged for cannibalism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T18:17:43-07:00","id":480977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/480378-the-west-other-supernaturals-in-the-wyld-west#post480378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since today is the 155th Anniversary of the Pony Express. I'm expanding on what the Wyld West books suggested. How do you run the other settings in the Wyld West?<br /> <br /> Here's my thing.<br /> <br /> Vampire: St. Louis is about as far west they want to risk going to. They stay on the eastern side of the country at all times. Those who risk heading west has it coming to them.<br /> Mage: They combat the Storm Umbra in their own ways. The Sons of Ether are on the rise and about to split from the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on the time period you are talking Voltarian Order or the Electrodyne engineers who don't split off until 1904.<br /> I think both favored forces but not sure. The Etherites are also have strong solfacti component so thats where they get the matter specialization.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T18:32:38-07:00","id":480988,"title":"","content":"There can be splinters, some of them going rogue either due to the Storm Umbra or the isolation the West provided.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T21:23:25-07:00","id":481105,"title":"","content":"I personally love the idea of Etherites and Technocrats being part of the &quot;Mystery Airship&quot; phenomena. That thesis formed a central part of a Werewolf the Wyld West game I ran years ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mystery_airship\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8e/Mystery_airship_SFCall_Nov_22_1896.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mystery_airship\" target=\"_blank\"> Mystery airship - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mystery_airship\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mystery_airship </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T21:50:50-07:00","id":481113,"title":"","content":"Gettysburg Wraiths and probably some Maelstrom due the death of the indian americans and such<br /> Demons: probably not, but A LOT OF APOCALYPSE/DOOMSDAY CULTS!<br /> Hunters: Probably hunters hunted and a lot of hunters welding faith<br /> Mages: Ohh boy, we have an interesting setting here. Gunslinger Mages :P and think about all the traditions exploring the native american culture and influence (And Drugs!)<br /> Fomori: look at werewolf<br /> Werewolf: i think we have a book about that already<br /> Vampires: probably a lot of them in major cities, i dont see vampires strolling down the deserts.<br /> Changelings:i dont run changeling..but i can see it somehow working with all the gunslingers mythos and such, and with the wild west mythos (John Henry!)<br /> Mummies: I dont run mummies thanks to god<br /> Technocracy: taking a clue from Deadlands, i see them bein the Men in Black or goverment officials.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T02:48:16-07:00","id":481236,"title":"","content":"For Mage there is a whole setting detailed in the Storyteller's Handbook. Victorian Age Vampire is pretty much the Vampire variant, and it would be pretty easy to transfer to the budding cities and politics Back East. I don't see a lot of interest by the Vampires for the actual West.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T09:12:43-07:00","id":481358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/480378-the-west-other-supernaturals-in-the-wyld-west?p=480977#post480977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on the time period you are talking Voltarian Order or the Electrodyne engineers who don't split off until 1904.<br /> I think both favored forces but not sure. The Etherites are also have strong solfacti component so thats where they get the matter specialization.</div> </div> </div> </div>The big experiment that pissed off the Electrodyne Engineers didn't take place until 1887. So there are effectively two periods in play for those-who-will-be-Etherites in the &quot;Old West&quot;: 1) between the end of the Civil War when the mass expansion to the West really took place where the Engineers are probably as happy with the Technocracy as the other Conventions and 2) around and after Michelson-Morely and ether being &quot;disproved&quot; and they start getting tetchy, though not so tetchy that they are not still &quot;playing adequately well with others&quot; since it takes about two decades to actually defect.<br /> <br /> The Voltarians were renamed to the Electrodyne Engineers in the foundations of the Union in 1851, which is a little before the early end of most conceptions of an Old West era game. <br /> <br /> But there aren't any actual Sons of Ether in the West as such, and their predecessors would have tended more to the Union than the Traditions. The Traditions don't have any real bent toward technomagic at this point. Even being kinda-sorta technological is frowned on, e.g. the Order of of Hermes kicking one of the founding Houses to the curb, for being, ya know, blacksmiths.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T09:23:15-07:00","id":481362,"title":"","content":"I had a portion of one of my Mage games take place in St. Louis in the 1870's. (The PCs were traveling home backwards in time from the future and overshot the mark.) I remember writing up a short &quot;position&quot; paper on how the Eight Traditions were different to hand out to the players. (Which I still have around here somewhere.) Stuff they would pick up on pretty quickly. Plus one player had left his character in the future, so he made up a new 19th century character that was going to join their cabal. They were intensively involved in the supernaturals of the city, so I also backdated each of the supernaturals they had dealt with previously. Some of the wraiths they knew were still alive. The vampires were under the thumb of the previous Prince and the modern Prince was a member of the primogen. They had met the City Spirit and the ended up meeting it's earlier iteration. I had dropped enough Easter Eggs throughout the game that a lot of mysteries were revealed. &quot;So THAT is why that NPC acted in that way!&quot; and &quot;So that's why this wraith acted like he already knew me when we first met!&quot; I was a ton of fun. Made me want to do a whole period piece game. I've toyed with going back and doing a Victorian/Wyld West one based on fond memories, but we've settled on the Roaring 20s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T19:43:08-07:00","id":481870,"title":"","content":"Wraith did have a Wyld West book; Ghost Towns. Midnight Express also deals with a wild west ghost town in Wraith terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T08:09:01-07:00","id":482364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/480378-the-west-other-supernaturals-in-the-wyld-west?p=481113#post481113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires: probably a lot of them in major cities, i dont see vampires strolling down the deserts.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/480378-the-west-other-supernaturals-in-the-wyld-west#post480378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire: St. Louis is about as far west they want to risk going to. They stay on the eastern side of the country at all times. Those who risk heading west has it coming to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the film &quot;Near Dark&quot; covered how Vampires would survive in a 'Old West' setting (even though the film took place in the 1980s when it was made) would be like so I can perfectly see Vampires in the west. Also I would like to have the existence of Vampires who are gunfighters/outlaws/bandits especially Native American Vampires who were possibly there before Europeans....<br /> <br /> Maybe perhaps there's Vampires who might even live or have their own personal trains (operated by their ghouls) that go town to town possibly...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5708,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5708-tunnelsofdarkness","user":"TunnelsofDarkness","date":". 04-16-2015, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5708-tunnelsofdarkness","name":"TunnelsofDarkness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T10:18:42-07:00","id":482507,"title":"","content":"I have some roaming in the American West among Sabbat attached to Indian tribes in the Great Plains and Din\u00e9 territory as part of my vampire character's backstory, though I've never actually played him in that setting. I'd imagine having a decent proficiency with Protean would be crucial for vampires on the frontier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T12:28:38-07:00","id":482636,"title":"","content":"I played in a great vampire game set during the founding of the Oregon territory that ran through to the early 1900s. Lots of Anarch influence as they struggled to start to build the Free State.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T12:58:05-07:00","id":482653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/480378-the-west-other-supernaturals-in-the-wyld-west?p=482507#post482507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some roaming in the American West among Sabbat attached to Indian tribes in the Great Plains and Din\u00e9 territory as part of my vampire character's backstory, though I've never actually played him in that setting. I'd imagine having a decent proficiency with Protean would be crucial for vampires on the frontier.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could have sedentary vampires pretty easily as well. Even though rifles and horses had moved many/most of the tribes out onto the Plains there were still some very sedentary ones and, with some of them, having Protean would get you found out and killed a lot faster (Skinwalker! Sorcerer!) than just hanging around sleeping in the day and only coming out at night (living in a dead man's house that has been sealed up, being the guy who lives in the kiva as its keeper, etc.)<br /> <br /> It would be difficult, but not too difficult to get a vamp with a coffin or other container out west either. The trails would have worked. You could definitely fit a full size coffin on a Conestoga wagon. People certainly did. A lead-lined coffin full of brine was used to take bodies down the Oregon trail. And repeatedly opened (while hymns were sung) to show the body to the Indians (who then let the very weird people pass through their territory ASAP). Going by steamboat up the rivers would have been easier. And once they are where they want to be, they just set up like normal. <br /> <br /> The density, like the population as a whole, would be pretty low. It would hard to have a whole coterie most places. But you could definitely have vamps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T13:04:50-07:00","id":482663,"title":"","content":"Oregon trail by night!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T13:06:44-07:00","id":482665,"title":"","content":"Santa Fe Trail might be more interesting. It went more places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T10:25:48-07:00","id":486494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/480378-the-west-other-supernaturals-in-the-wyld-west?p=482653#post482653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">with some of them, having Protean would get you found out and killed a lot faster (Skinwalker! Sorcerer!) than just hanging around sleeping in the day and only coming out at night (living in a dead man's house that has been sealed up, being the guy who lives in the kiva as its keeper, etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm skeptical about this. Remember that while you're &quot;sleeping&quot; in the day you are to all appearances dead, and doing so where others could find you could easily result in a fiery death if someone moves your body for burial or lets in a stray sunbeam through an entrance at the wrong time. Showing up each night from an unknown location seems more secure to me than hoping no one stumbles across you during the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T16:01:07-07:00","id":486789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/480378-the-west-other-supernaturals-in-the-wyld-west?p=486494#post486494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm skeptical about this. Remember that while you're &quot;sleeping&quot; in the day you are to all appearances dead, and doing so where others could find you could easily result in a fiery death if someone moves your body for burial or lets in a stray sunbeam through an entrance at the wrong time. Showing up each night from an unknown location seems more secure to me than hoping no one stumbles across you during the day.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about just having a job where you stay in one place during the day and are only expected to do things at night? Or can avoid going outside unless you want to b/c your job is inside, just keep a high humanity and you can keep active enough to do the right ceremony when necessary? Or hanging out in homes where someone died, so they have been ceremonially closed and abandoned? <br /> <br /> However, pop claws, melt into the ground, change shape or turn into mist and you are the worst of the worst. No effort, absolutely none, will be spared by the most mystically ept people in the community to end you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T22:09:08-07:00","id":487048,"title":"","content":"That doesn't make any more sense to me than werewolves' default kill-on-sight attitude toward vampires in the CWoD. Revealing yourself as a supernatural creature (and surely any Gangrel worth their tailfeathers should be able to avoid having witnesses trail them to their resting place) would no doubt cause some mix of fear and awe, but I can't recall a Native American culture that lacked benevolent and capricious spirits/creatures to go along with the malevolent ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T09:37:01-07:00","id":487346,"title":"","content":"Sorcerers, witches and skin-walkers were arguably human. Some might have been some form of shapechanger (though they usually had several forms in their repetoires and typically they were not ones always associated with known shifter-types). Others might have been Gangrel. I'm betting they were probably more sophisticated about what supernaturals were what and the various ways to deal with them. No Masquerade to obfuscate issues and all. <br /> <br /> Sure supernaturals would be tough foes, but there wasn't anything resembling a Rule of Shade for the Native American Dreamspeakers (or depending on how ecumenical the Traditions were in the mid-19th century, probably Verbena, possibly Euthanatoi, potentially Celestial Choristers, particularly among those who had adopted some version of Christianity) would have been front and center in their communities. <br /> <br /> Vamps would have had a much easier time with more sedentary groups. So Native Gangrel might have had some association with the more mobile tribes of the Plains. Though most of those groups were sedentary a couple of generations before, so any vamps in situ would have had to adapt fast to a more mobilized society. (And probably didn't.... just got left behind, starve and went into torpor, as a best case scenario). Vamps among the Pueblo Peoples would have had an easier time of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T16:39:27-07:00","id":487788,"title":"","content":"There Wyld West book about Mexico covers the Sabbat there in detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T00:07:30-07:00","id":489127,"title":"","content":"@ Matt: It's something I've tried before, how to incoporate other settings into a certain time period. Other than the anniversary I have three historical setting books, Wyld West, Sorcerer's Crusade, and Great War. I went with Wyld West cause of the three books, it's smaller, an updated timeline, and the anniversary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}